  "oral_argument": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Paul D. Clement",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9928e2a69e79bc54a6f8e2ec35d6f5e64958880512ba94f5c8efcffefb634aaf",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9928e2a69e79-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 19,
              "start": 19
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Paul D. Clement argued that the 1995 amendment to Section\u202f409 is constitutional and protects data used for federal highway funding from litigation."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "United States Government",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9928e2a69e79bc54a6f8e2ec35d6f5e64958880512ba94f5c8efcffefb634aaf",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9928e2a69e79-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to United States Government, the United States Government questioned whether the 409 privilege depends on a state\u2019s assertion of the privilege to receive funding, emphasizing that the privilege serves a federal interest in accurate information."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court Transcript",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9928e2a69e79bc54a6f8e2ec35d6f5e64958880512ba94f5c8efcffefb634aaf",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9928e2a69e79-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 25,
              "start": 25
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court noted that federal highway funds and the documents used for that purpose have an inherently federal character, giving Congress power to protect them in litigation."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court Transcript",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9928e2a69e79bc54a6f8e2ec35d6f5e64958880512ba94f5c8efcffefb634aaf",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9928e2a69e79-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court stated that the act must have authority under some Article\u202fI, Section\u202f(a) basis."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. MUNGIA",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9928e2a69e79bc54a6f8e2ec35d6f5e64958880512ba94f5c8efcffefb634aaf",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9928e2a69e79-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 40,
              "start": 40
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Mr. Mungia argued that there is no final judgment in the tort action and that the discovery order was taken up on interlocutory appeal."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. MUNGIA",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9928e2a69e79bc54a6f8e2ec35d6f5e64958880512ba94f5c8efcffefb634aaf",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9928e2a69e79-0002-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 46,
              "start": 46
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Mr. Mungia also argued that the funding condition cannot be authorized under the Spending Clause."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. MUNGIA",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9928e2a69e79bc54a6f8e2ec35d6f5e64958880512ba94f5c8efcffefb634aaf",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9928e2a69e79-0002-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 48,
              "start": 48
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. MUNGIA, the statutory language requires control over vehicle size and weight to avoid loss of funding, similar to other statutes."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9928e2a69e79bc54a6f8e2ec35d6f5e64958880512ba94f5c8efcffefb634aaf",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9928e2a69e79-0002-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 49,
              "start": 49
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court referenced the Dole case, noting that under 23\u202fU.S.C.\u202f158 the title of the act was withdrawal of Federal funds."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Solicitor General",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9928e2a69e79bc54a6f8e2ec35d6f5e64958880512ba94f5c8efcffefb634aaf",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9928e2a69e79-0002-0008"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 55,
              "start": 55
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Solicitor General, as amicus, argued that documents in the hands of the transferee agency are protected because they exist only due to the planning agency\u2019s collection of that information."
      }
    ],
